{"id":"mahabharata-3-275","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":275,"title":"पञ्चसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 275 · Sita's vindication and Rama's return","summary":{"en":"Sita is brought to Rama, who at first refuses to take her back; the Wind, Fire, Varuna and Brahma declare her pure, and Dasharatha appears from heaven to bless his son. Rama crowns Vibhishana, returns in the Pushpaka chariot to Ayodhya, is joyfully received by Bharata, and rules, performing ten horse sacrifices on the Gomati.","kn":"ಸೀತೆಯನ್ನು ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನ ಬಳಿಗೆ ತರಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ಮೊದಲು ಅವನು ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸಲು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವಾಯು, ಅಗ್ನಿ, ವರುಣ, ಬ್ರಹ್ಮರು ಅವಳು ಪರಿಶುದ್ಧಳೆಂದು ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ದಶರಥನು ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಿಂದ ಬಂದು ಮಗನನ್ನು ಆಶೀರ್ವದಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಭೀಷಣನಿಗೆ ಪಟ್ಟಗಟ್ಟಿ ಪುಷ್ಪಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಯೋಧ್ಯೆಗೆ ಮರಳಿ ಭರತನಿಂದ ಹರ್ಷದಿಂದ ಸ್ವಾಗತಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟು ಗೋಮತೀ ತೀರದಲ್ಲಿ ಹತ್ತು ಅಶ್ವಮೇಧಗಳನ್ನು ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾ ಆಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सीता को श्रीराम के पास लाया जाता है, जो पहले उन्हें स्वीकार करने से मना करते हैं; वायु, अग्नि, वरुण और ब्रह्मा उन्हें पवित्र घोषित करते हैं, और दशरथ स्वर्ग से आकर पुत्र को आशीर्वाद देते हैं। श्रीराम विभीषण का अभिषेक कर पुष्पक विमान से अयोध्या लौटते हैं, भरत उनका हर्ष से स्वागत करते हैं, और वे गोमती के तट पर दस अश्वमेध करते हुए राज्य करते हैं।","te":"సీతను శ్రీరాముని దగ్గరకు తెస్తారు, మొదట అతడు స్వీకరించడానికి నిరాకరిస్తాడు; వాయువు, అగ్ని, వరుణుడు, బ్రహ్మ ఆమె పవిత్రురాలని ప్రకటిస్తారు, దశరథుడు స్వర్గం నుండి వచ్చి కుమారుని ఆశీర్వదిస్తాడు. విభీషణునికి పట్టం కట్టి పుష్పకంలో అయోధ్యకు తిరిగివచ్చి భరతుని చేత ఆనందంగా స్వాగతం పొంది గోమతీ తీరంలో పది అశ్వమేధాలు చేస్తూ పాలిస్తాడు.","ta":"ஸீதை ஸ்ரீராமரிடம் கொணரப்பட, முதலில் அவர் ஏற்க மறுக்கிறார்; வாயு, அக்னி, வருணன், ப்ரஹ்மா அவள் தூயவள் என்று அறிவிக்க, தஶரதன் ஸ்வர்க்கத்திலிருந்து வந்து மகனை ஆசீர்வதிக்கிறான். விபீஷணனுக்கு முடிசூட்டிப் புஷ்பக விமானத்தில் அயோத்தி திரும்பிப் பரதனால் மகிழ்வுடன் வரவேற்கப்பட்டுக் கோமதிக் கரையில் பத்து அஶ்வமேதங்கள் செய்து ஆள்கிறார்.","ml":"സീതയെ രാമന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തിക്കുന്നു; ആദ്യം അദ്ദേഹം അവളെ സ്വീകരിക്കാൻ വിസമ്മതിക്കുന്നു; വായു, അഗ്നി, വരുണൻ, ബ്രഹ്മാവ് എന്നിവർ അവൾ നിർമ്മലയെന്ന് പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; മകനെ അനുഗ്രഹിക്കാൻ ദശരഥൻ സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിൽനിന്ന് പ്രത്യക്ഷനാകുന്നു. രാമൻ വിഭീഷണനെ കിരീടമണിയിക്കുന്നു, പുഷ്പകവിമാനത്തിൽ അയോധ്യയിലേക്ക് മടങ്ങുന്നു; ഭരതൻ സന്തോഷത്തോടെ സ്വീകരിക്കുന്നു; ഗോമതീതീരത്ത് പത്ത് അശ്വമേധയാഗങ്ങൾ നടത്തി അദ്ദേഹം ഭരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.275; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स हत्वा रावणं क्षुद्रं राक्षसेन्द्रं सुरद्विषम् ।\nबभूव हृष्टः ससुहृद्रामः सौमित्रिणा सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed the base Ravana, lord of the rakshasas and enemy of the gods, Rama rejoiced with his friends and Lakshmana."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो हते दशग्रीवे देवाः सर्षिपुरोगमाः ।\nआशीर्भिर्जययुक्ताभिरानर्चुस्तं महाभुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the ten-necked one was dead, the gods led by the sages honored the mighty-armed Rama with blessings of victory."}},{"n":3,"text":"रामं कमलपत्राक्षं तुष्टुवुः सर्वदेवताः ।\nगन्धर्वाः पुष्पवर्षैश्च वाग्भिश्च त्रिदशालयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the gods praised lotus-eyed Rama, and the gandharvas, dwellers of heaven, honored him with showers of flowers and with words."}},{"n":4,"text":"पूजयित्वा यथा रामं प्रतिजग्मुर्यथागतम् ।\nतन्महोत्सवसंकाशमासीदाकाशमच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honored Rama as was fitting, they went back as they had come, and the sky seemed like a great festival, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो हत्वा दशग्रीवं लङ्कां रामो महायशाः ।\nविभीषणाय प्रददौ प्रभुः परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After killing Ravana, the greatly renowned Rama, the lord who conquers enemy cities, gave Lanka to Vibhishana."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः सीतां पुरस्कृत्य विभीषणपुरस्कृताम् ।\nअविन्ध्यो नाम सुप्रज्ञो वृद्धामात्यो विनिर्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very wise old minister Avindhya came out, bringing Sita, with Vibhishana going before her."}},{"n":7,"text":"उवाच च महात्मानं काकुत्स्थं दैन्यमास्थितम् ।\nप्रतीच्छ देवीं सद्वृत्तां महात्मञ्जानकीमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to the great-souled Rama, who was in a sorrowful mood: \"Great soul, take back the lady Janaki, of good conduct.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा वचस्तस्मादवतीर्य रथोत्तमात् ।\nबाष्पेणापिहितां सीतां ददर्शेक्ष्वाकुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Rama, delight of the Ikshvakus, got down from the excellent chariot and saw Sita, her face hidden by tears."}},{"n":9,"text":"तां दृष्ट्वा चारुसर्वाङ्गीं यानस्थां शोककर्शिताम् ।\nमलोपचितसर्वाङ्गीं जटिलां कृष्णवाससम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her, lovely in every limb but wasted with grief, seated in a vehicle, with her limbs covered with dirt, matted hair, and dark clothes,"}},{"n":10,"text":"उवाच रामो वैदेहीं परामर्शविशङ्कितः ।\nगच्छ वैदेहि मुक्ता त्वं यत्कार्यं तन्मया कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, suspicious on reflection, said to Sita: \"Go, Sita; you are free. I have done what had to be done."}},{"n":11,"text":"मामासाद्य पतिं भद्रे न त्वं राक्षसवेश्मनि ।\nजरां व्रजेथा इति मे निहतोऽसौ निशाचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good lady, I killed that night-wanderer so that, having me for a husband, you would not grow old in a rakshasa's house."}},{"n":12,"text":"कथं ह्यस्मद्विधो जातु जानन्धर्मविनिश्चयम् ।\nपरहस्तगतां नारीं मुहूर्तमपि धारयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could a man like me, who knows the rule of dharma, keep for even a moment a woman who has been in another's hands?"}},{"n":13,"text":"सुवृत्तामसुवृत्तां वाप्यहं त्वामद्य मैथिलि ।\nनोत्सहे परिभोगाय श्वावलीढं हविर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether your conduct has been good or not, Maithili, I cannot take you to myself, like an oblation licked by a dog.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः सा सहसा बाला तच्छ्रुत्वा दारुणं वचः ।\nपपात देवी व्यथिता निकृत्ता कदली यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those cruel words, the young lady suddenly fell, pained, like a cut plantain tree."}},{"n":15,"text":"यो ह्यस्या हर्षसंभूतो मुखरागस्तदाभवत् ।\nक्षणेन स पुनर्भ्रष्टो निःश्वासादिव दर्पणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glow that had come to her face from joy vanished again in an instant, like breath on a mirror."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततस्ते हरयः सर्वे तच्छ्रुत्वा रामभाषितम् ।\nगतासुकल्पा निश्चेष्टा बभूवुः सहलक्ष्मणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the monkeys, hearing what Rama said, became like dead men, motionless, together with Lakshmana."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततो देवो विशुद्धात्मा विमानेन चतुर्मुखः ।\nपितामहो जगत्स्रष्टा दर्शयामास राघवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the pure-souled god, the four-faced Brahma, creator of the world, grandfather, showed himself to Rama in a celestial car."}},{"n":18,"text":"शक्रश्चाग्निश्च वायुश्च यमो वरुण एव च ।\nयक्षाधिपश्च भगवांस्तथा सप्तर्षयोऽमलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, Agni, Vayu, Yama, Varuna, the blessed lord of the yakshas, and the spotless seven sages also appeared."}},{"n":19,"text":"राजा दशरथश्चैव दिव्यभास्वरमूर्तिमान् ।\nविमानेन महार्हेण हंसयुक्तेन भास्वता ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Dasharatha too appeared in a shining divine form, in a splendid, costly aerial car drawn by swans."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षं तत्सर्वं देवगन्धर्वसंकुलम् ।\nशुशुभे तारकाचित्रं शरदीव नभस्तलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the whole sky, filled with gods and gandharvas, shone like the autumn heavens with their many stars."}},{"n":21,"text":"तत उत्थाय वैदेहि तेषां मध्ये यशस्विनी ।\nउवाच वाक्यं कल्याणी रामं पृथुलवक्षसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the renowned, auspicious lady of Videha rose among them and spoke to Rama of broad chest:"}},{"n":22,"text":"राजपुत्र न ते कोपं करोमि विदिता हि मे ।\nगतिः स्त्रीणां नराणां च शृणु चेदं वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Prince, I am not angry with you, for I know the ways of women and men. Hear this speech of mine."}},{"n":23,"text":"अन्तश्चरति भूतानां मातरिश्वा सदागतिः ।\nस मे विमुञ्चतु प्राणान्यदि पापं चराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vayu, the wind that always moves, travels within all beings; let him take my life if I have done any wrong."}},{"n":24,"text":"अग्निरापस्तथाकाशं पृथिवी वायुरेव च ।\nविमुञ्चन्तु मम प्राणान्यदि पापं चराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire, water, space, earth, and air: let them take my life if I have done any wrong.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षे वागासीत्सर्वा विश्रावयन्दिशः ।\nपुण्या संहर्षणी तेषां वानराणां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a voice rang through the sky, making all directions hear, pure and delighting those great monkeys."}},{"text":"वायुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vayu said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"भो भो राघव सत्यं वै वायुरस्मि सदागतिः ।\nअपापा मैथिली राजन्संगच्छ सह भार्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O Raghava, I am Vayu, the ever-moving, and I tell you truly: Maithili is without sin, king. Take your wife back.\""}},{"text":"अग्निरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Agni said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"अहमन्तःशरीरस्थो भूतानां रघुनन्दन ।\nसुसूक्ष्ममपि काकुत्स्थ मैथिली नापराध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Delight of the Raghus, I dwell within the bodies of beings. Kakutstha, Maithili has done no wrong, not even the smallest.\""}},{"text":"वरुण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Varuna said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"रसा वै मत्प्रसूता हि भूतदेहेषु राघव ।\nअहं वै त्वां प्रब्रवीमि मैथिली प्रतिगृह्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Raghava, the sap in the bodies of creatures comes from me. I tell you, take Maithili back.\""}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"पुत्र नैतदिहाश्चर्यं त्वयि राजर्षिधर्मिणि ।\nसाधो सद्वृत्तमार्गस्थे शृणु चेदं वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My son, this is no wonder in you, a royal sage in dharma, a good man on the path of right conduct. Hear my words."}},{"n":30,"text":"शत्रुरेष त्वया वीर देवगन्धर्वभोगिनाम् ।\nयक्षाणां दानवानां च महर्षीणां च पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This enemy of gods, gandharvas, serpents, yakshas, danavas, and great sages has been struck down by you, hero."}},{"n":31,"text":"अवध्यः सर्वभूतानां मत्प्रसादात्पुराभवत् ।\nकस्माच्चित्कारणात्पापः कंचित्कालमुपेक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By my favor he was long ago unkillable by any creature, and for some reason I let that wicked one go for a time."}},{"n":32,"text":"वधार्थमात्मनस्तेन हृता सीता दुरात्मना ।\nनलकूबरशापेन रक्षा चास्याः कृता मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"That evil one carried off Sita for his own death. I protected her by the curse of Nalakubara."}},{"n":33,"text":"यदि ह्यकामामासेवेत्स्त्रियमन्यामपि ध्रुवम् ।\nशतधास्य फलेद्देह इत्युक्तः सोऽभवत्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For he had been told: 'If you take any unwilling woman, your body will split into a hundred pieces.'"}},{"n":34,"text":"नात्र शङ्का त्वया कार्या प्रतीच्छेमां महाद्युते ।\nकृतं त्वया महत्कार्यं देवानाममरप्रभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"You must not doubt here. Take her back, radiant one. You have done a great work for the gods, immortal in splendor.\""}},{"text":"दशरथ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dasharatha said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"प्रीतोऽस्मि वत्स भद्रं ते पिता दशरथोऽस्मि ते ।\nअनुजानामि राज्यं च प्रशाधि पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased, child; blessings on you. I am your father Dasharatha. I give you leave: rule the kingdom, best of men.\""}},{"text":"राम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rama said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"अभिवादये त्वां राजेन्द्र यदि त्वं जनको मम ।\nगमिष्यामि पुरीं रम्यामयोध्यां शासनात्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I salute you, king of kings, if you are indeed my father. At your command I will go to the lovely city of Ayodhya.\""}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"तमुवाच पिता भूयः प्रहृष्टो मनुजाधिप ।\nगच्छायोध्यां प्रशाधि त्वं राम रक्तान्तलोचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then his father, greatly pleased, said to him again, lord of men: \"Go to Ayodhya and rule, Rama, red-cornered eyes.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"ततो देवान्नमस्कृत्य सुहृद्भिरभिनन्दितः ।\nमहेन्द्र इव पौलोम्या भार्यया स समेयिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama bowed to the gods, was congratulated by his friends, and was united with his wife, like Mahendra with Paulomi."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततो वरं ददौ तस्मै अविन्ध्याय परंतपः ।\nत्रिजटां चार्थमानाभ्यां योजयामास राक्षसीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that tamer of foes gave Avindhya a boon, and joined the rakshasi Trijata with wealth and honor."}},{"n":40,"text":"तमुवाच ततो ब्रह्मा देवैः शक्रमुखैर्वृतः ।\nकौसल्यामातरिष्टांस्ते वरानद्य ददानि कान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brahma, surrounded by the gods led by Indra, said to him: \"Son of Kaushalya, what desired boons shall I give you today?\""}},{"n":41,"text":"वव्रे रामः स्थितिं धर्मे शत्रुभिश्चापराजयम् ।\nराक्षसैर्निहतानां च वानराणां समुद्भवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama chose steadfastness in dharma, and not to be defeated by enemies, and the revival of the monkeys killed by rakshasas."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्ते ब्रह्मणा प्रोक्ते तथेति वचने तदा ।\nसमुत्तस्थुर्महाराज वानरा लब्धचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, at Brahma's word \"So be it,\" the monkeys got up, restored to consciousness."}},{"n":43,"text":"सीता चापि महाभागा वरं हनुमते ददौ ।\nरामकीर्त्या समं पुत्र जीवितं ते भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very fortunate Sita also gave a boon to Hanuman: \"Your life will last as long as Rama's fame, my son."}},{"n":44,"text":"दिव्यास्त्वामुपभोगाश्च मत्प्रसादकृताः सदा ।\nउपस्थास्यन्ति हनुमन्निति स्म हरिलोचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"And divine pleasures given by my favor will always wait upon you, Hanuman,\" she said to the monkey."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततस्ते प्रेक्षमाणानां तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nअन्तर्धानं ययुर्देवाः सर्वे शक्रपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as those men of untiring deeds looked on, all the gods led by Indra vanished."}},{"n":46,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु रामं जानक्या समेतं शक्रसारथिः ।\nउवाच परमप्रीतः सुहृन्मध्य इदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Rama reunited with Janaki, Indra's charioteer, greatly pleased, spoke these words among his friends:"}},{"n":47,"text":"देवगन्धर्वयक्षाणां मानुषासुरभोगिनाम् ।\nअपनीतं त्वया दुःखमिदं सत्यपराक्रम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By you, of true valor, this grief of the gods, gandharvas, yakshas, humans, asuras, and serpents has been removed."}},{"n":48,"text":"सदेवासुरगन्धर्वा यक्षराक्षसपन्नगाः ।\nकथयिष्यन्ति लोकास्त्वां यावद्भूमिर्धरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, asuras, gandharvas, yakshas, rakshasas, and serpents will speak of you as long as the earth endures.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"इत्येवमुक्त्वानुज्ञाप्य रामं शस्त्रभृतां वरम् ।\nसंपूज्यापाक्रमत्तेन रथेनादित्यवर्चसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, and taken leave of Rama, best of the armed, and honored him, Matali drove away in that sun-bright chariot."}},{"n":50,"text":"ततः सीतां पुरस्कृत्य रामः सौमित्रिणा सह ।\nसुग्रीवप्रमुखैश्चैव सहितः सर्ववानरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama with Lakshmana, putting Sita in front, and with all the monkeys led by Sugriva,"}},{"n":51,"text":"विधाय रक्षां लङ्कायां विभीषणपुरस्कृतः ।\nसंततार पुनस्तेन सेतुना मकरालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"having set up Lanka's protection, with Vibhishana before him, crossed again over the sea by that bridge."}},{"n":52,"text":"पुष्पकेण विमानेन खेचरेण विराजता ।\nकामगेन यथा मुख्यैरमात्यैः संवृतो वशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Self-controlled, he traveled in the Pushpaka aerial car, shining and moving at will in the sky, surrounded by his chief ministers."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततस्तीरे समुद्रस्य यत्र शिश्ये स पार्थिवः ।\nतत्रैवोवास धर्मात्मा सहितः सर्ववानरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then on the seashore where the king had lain down, there the righteous one stayed with all the monkeys."}},{"n":54,"text":"अथैनान्राघवः काले समानीयाभिपूज्य च ।\nविसर्जयामास तदा रत्नैः संतोष्य सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at the proper time Rama gathered and honored them, satisfied them all with jewels, and sent them away."}},{"n":55,"text":"गतेषु वानरेन्द्रेषु गोपुच्छर्क्षेषु तेषु च ।\nसुग्रीवसहितो रामः किष्किन्धां पुनरागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the monkey lords, the cow-tailed apes, and the bears had gone, Rama with Sugriva returned to Kishkindha."}},{"n":56,"text":"विभीषणेनानुगतः सुग्रीवसहितस्तदा ।\nपुष्पकेण विमानेन वैदेह्या दर्शयन्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Followed by Vibhishana and with Sugriva, he went in the Pushpaka car, showing Sita the forest."}},{"n":57,"text":"किष्किन्धां तु समासाद्य रामः प्रहरतां वरः ।\nअङ्गदं कृतकर्माणं यौवराज्येऽभ्यषेचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Kishkindha, Rama, best of fighters, consecrated Angada, who had done his work, as heir apparent."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततस्तैरेव सहितो रामः सौमित्रिणा सह ।\nयथागतेन मार्गेण प्रययौ स्वपुरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with those same companions and with Lakshmana, Rama went by the way he had come to his own city."}},{"n":59,"text":"अयोध्यां स समासाद्य पुरीं राष्ट्रपतिस्ततः ।\nभरताय हनूमन्तं दूतं प्रस्थापयत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the city of Ayodhya, the lord of the realm sent Hanuman as a messenger to Bharata."}},{"n":60,"text":"लक्षयित्वेङ्गितं सर्वं प्रियं तस्मै निवेद्य च ।\nवायुपुत्रे पुनः प्राप्ते नन्दिग्राममुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having read all the signs, he told Bharata the good news, and when the son of the wind returned, Rama went to Nandigrama."}},{"n":61,"text":"स तत्र मलदिग्धाङ्गं भरतं चीरवाससम् ।\nअग्रतः पादुके कृत्वा ददर्शासीनमासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw Bharata, his limbs smeared with dirt and wearing bark clothes, seated on a seat with the sandals before him."}},{"n":62,"text":"समेत्य भरतेनाथ शत्रुघ्नेन च वीर्यवान् ।\nराघवः सहसौमित्रिर्मुमुदे भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting Bharata and Shatrughna, the mighty Raghava with Lakshmana rejoiced, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":63,"text":"तथा भरतशत्रुघ्नौ समेतौ गुरुणा तदा ।\nवैदेह्या दर्शनेनोभौ प्रहर्षं समवापतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata and Shatrughna, united with their elder, were both overjoyed at seeing Sita."}},{"n":64,"text":"तस्मै तद्भरतो राज्यमागतायाभिसत्कृतम् ।\nन्यासं निर्यातयामास युक्तः परमया मुदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, with great joy, honored him on his return and handed back the kingdom held in trust."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततस्तं वैष्णवे शूरं नक्षत्रेऽभिमतेऽहनि ।\nवसिष्ठो वामदेवश्च सहितावभ्यषिञ्चताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vasishtha and Vamadeva together consecrated that hero on a day with the Vaishnava star that he liked."}},{"n":66,"text":"सोऽभिषिक्तः कपिश्रेष्ठं सुग्रीवं ससुहृज्जनम् ।\nविभीषणं च पौलस्त्यमन्वजानाद्गृहान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once consecrated, he gave leave to Sugriva, the best of monkeys, with his friends, and to Vibhishana, the descendant of Pulastya, to return home."}},{"n":67,"text":"अभ्यर्च्य विविधै रत्नैः प्रीतियुक्तौ मुदा युतौ ।\nसमाधायेतिकर्तव्यं दुःखेन विससर्ज ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoring both with many jewels, they were glad and joyful; arranging what was to be done, he sent them off with sorrow."}},{"n":68,"text":"पुष्पकं च विमानं तत्पूजयित्वा स राघवः ।\nप्रादाद्वैश्रवणायैव प्रीत्या स रघुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama also honored the Pushpaka car and gladly gave it back to Kubera, son of Vishravas."}},{"n":69,"text":"ततो देवर्षिसहितः सरितं गोमतीमनु ।\nदशाश्वमेधानाजह्रे जारूथ्यान्स निरर्गलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with sages and gods, along the Gomati river, he performed ten unobstructed horse sacrifices, ending with the final bath."}}]}]}